  "id": "galactosemia",
  "term": "galactosemia",
  "definition": "Galactosemia is a group of inherited enzyme disorders in which galactose builds up in the blood. The classic form begins in infancy and can involve poor growth, vomiting, increased pressure inside the skull, and later problems such as jaundice, enlarged liver and spleen, cataracts, intellectual disability, and ovarian failure.",
